    ],
    "text": "HOSPITAL UPGRADING OF MINISTRY OF HEALTH, NUTRITION AND INDIGENOUS MEDICINE",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      55.29,
      445.09,
      546.35,
      468.16
    ],
    "text": "AS proposed under the Budget Speech 2017, two new Medical Faculties were established in the Sabaragamuwa Universityof Sri Lanka and Wayamba University of Sri Lanka, with the aim of expanding medical education in Sri Lanka.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 0,
    "bbox": [
      55.29,
      481.09,
      546.39,
      528.16
    ],
    "text": "The Provincial General Hospital (PGH), Ratnapura and Base Hospital-Kuliyapitiya have been selected in orderto facilitate the clinical training for students of the new faculties. Accordingly, these two hospitals were upgraded asTeaching Hospitals with effect from the dates given below to develop the required facilities for under-graduate and post-graduate training.",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
